course: dictionary
lesson: 13187
title: A posh old-fashioned word: frightfully
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Frightfully is an old-fashioned British word. Most of the time it means very or extremely, as in «Thank you, that was frightfully kind.» It does not mean scary here, even though it looks like frightful.
explain: You will find it in older children's books. Toad in The Wind in the Willows talks like this, saying things like «frightfully good». When you read it, swap in very and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes frightfully means in a frightening or terrible way, as in «The car was frightfully crushed in the crash.» This is rarer. Look at the clues: if the sentence describes something bad, it probably means terrible, and if it describes a kind or polite feeling, it probably means very.
fact: Frightfully is an adverb, so it tells you more about another word, such as how kind or how sorry.
fact: «Frightfully» means very or extremely, as in «frightfully kind» or «frightfully sorry».
fact: «Frightfully» can also mean in a frightening or terrible way, as in «frightfully injured», which means badly hurt.
fact: Frightfully is mainly used in British English and sounds old-fashioned today.
fact: Do not confuse frightfully with frightening: the word can be posh, not scary.
exercise: «Thank you, that was frightfully kind.» What does frightfully mean here? | Scary | Quietly | Late | * Very
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to frightfully in «I am frightfully sorry»? | * Extremely | Sideways | Hungrily | Frightened
exercise: «The sailor was frightfully hurt in the storm.» What does frightfully suggest here? | * In a terrible way, badly | Quickly and quietly | Very happy | Just a little
test: What does frightfully mean in «I am frightfully sorry I broke your cup»? | Slowly | Scary-looking | Quietly | * Very, extremely
test: Ben reads «frightfully good» and thinks it means scary good. What is the best check? | * Swap in very good and see if the sentence still makes sense | Skip the whole sentence and forget it | Look for the word in a different book only | Ask someone to draw a picture
exam: Which sentence uses frightfully in the sense of in a terrible way? | The map was frightfully useful | * The car was frightfully crushed in the crash | The cake was frightfully good | The sun was frightfully warm on the beach
